let __v_10444 = Value::from("Aim for about ten or fewer in a window, and treat more than about twenty as a sign the work has no shape rather than a memory emergency: each tab costs a few tens of megabytes, and it is worth closing them once the machine starts swapping to disk. Group what belongs together - tab groups or a second window per project - pin the two or three you use all day, and close everything you opened to read later into a bookmark folder or a read-later list. If you keep losing the same kind of page, that is the one to pin rather than to keep finding it again.");
